sequenceDiagram
autonumber

actor FE as Frontend / Postman
participant GW as Gateway :8099
participant GSF as GatewaySecurityFilter
participant AUTH as Auth Service :8091
participant ACF as CompanyContextFilter
participant ADB as Auth DB

rect rgb(245,245,245)
Note over FE,ADB: Switch Company
FE->>GW: POST /api/v1/auth/switch-company\nAuthorization: Bearer ...\n{companyId OR companyCode}
GW->>GSF: Validate token
GSF->>GSF: Extract companyId claim\nInject X-Company-Id
GSF-->>GW: Continue
GW->>AUTH: Forward request
AUTH->>ACF: Resolve context (header/token)
AUTH->>ADB: Validate ACTIVE user-company mapping

alt Mapping valid
    AUTH->>AUTH: Generate NEW accessToken\nwith selected companyId
    AUTH->>ADB: Replace refresh token
    AUTH-->>GW: LoginData(defaultCompanyId=selected,\ncompanies[] isDefault updated)
    GW-->>FE: 200 Success
else Mapping invalid
    AUTH-->>GW: 400/401 invalid switch
    GW-->>FE: Error
end
end

rect rgb(245,245,245)
Note over FE,AUTH: Next API Call after Switch
FE->>FE: Replace old accessToken with new token
FE->>GW: POST protected endpoint + NEW token
GW->>GSF: Validate token + inject X-Company-Id(new)

alt New token used
    GW->>AUTH: /api/v1/auth/** OR /api/v1/setting/**
    AUTH->>ACF: CompanyContext = new companyId
else Old token still used
    GW->>AUTH: Request executes under old company
    AUTH-->>FE: Old company data appears
end
end

Note over FE,AUTH: Most common issue: frontend does not update Authorization header with NEW access token.
